+++ b/contrib/doodleverse/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-only -->
+
+# Doodleverse Core development fork
+
+This is an experimental independent Scrypt blockchain derived from Pepecoin
+Core v1.1.0, pinned to commit
+`4fb5a0cd930c0df82c88292e973a7b7cfa06c4e8`. It is development software for
+disposable test networks. Mainnet startup is disabled until a real native DVC
+founder receiving address is reviewed and pinned in consensus. The historical
+Ethereum-style `0x` address is not a native DVC destination.
+
+## Licensing
+
+Existing Bitcoin Core, Dogecoin Core and Pepecoin Core source retains its
+upstream MIT copyright and license notices, including the original root
+`COPYING` file. Those notices must be preserved when distributing the fork.
+
+New Doodleverse changes and the Doodle Tick build integration are published
+under the GNU General Public License, version 3 only (`GPL-3.0-only`). New
+Doodleverse-only files, including `genesis.py` and
+`src/test/doodleverse_tests.cpp`, carry that SPDX identifier. Retained upstream
+MIT notices do not constitute a new MIT grant for the Doodleverse additions.
+
+The complete GPLv3 text is in the Doodle Tick repository's root `LICENSE`
+and is included in its build artifacts. Distributions must include that text
+as well as the applicable upstream notices and corresponding source required
+by their licenses.
+
+## Network record and verification
+
+[chain-manifest.json](chain-manifest.json) records the protocol revision,
+genesis headers and hashes, Scrypt proofs, ports, network identifiers, address
+prefixes, supply limits and founder destination status. `mainnet_ready` is
+deliberately `false`. Testnet and regtest use a disclosed public test key for
+the founder allocation; anyone can spend those test coins. They are not a
+mainnet allocation or a claim of ownership.
+
+Run `python3 contrib/doodleverse/genesis.py --verify` from the source root to
+check the pinned genesis Scrypt proofs. Each genesis has a zero-value
+unspendable output. The exact founder allocation belongs to block 1 and is
+subject to normal coinbase maturity and chain rollback. Direct Scrypt mining
+is supported; AuxPoW is disabled.
+
+After compiling, run the `doodleverse_tests` and `scrypt_tests` Boost suites.
+The new suite checks supply, allocation rejection, maturity, fee limits,
+network isolation and founder UTXO rollback. The complete upstream test suite
+still contains Pepecoin-specific genesis, subsidy, address and AuxPoW
+expectations; its unchanged fixtures do not describe this fork. Source checks
+and genesis proof verification alone do not establish that a native build or
+network test passed.
